  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'You (the router) will be given an internal IP address, with format 192.168.x.x,
    and Subnet Mask 255.255.0.0. Each inbound packet will have a destination IP Address,
    indicating where the packet should go. Routers decide where to send the packet
    based on the packet IP Address and Subnet Mask. For example, the subnet mask
    255.255.0.0 means the first two numbers will identify the "subnet" that the packet
    is destined for. Therefore, any packets with IP starting ''192.168'' are destined
    for the home network.


    In this exercise, if the packet starts with ''192.168'',
    send it home by pressing ''A''.

    If the packet starts with anything else,
    send it to the internet by pressing ''D'''
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d9db2cc575f30f44784436c3920b5a52, type: 2}
